  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\nIssue Number 1, 2006\n\n## IMMEDIATE PASIPRESIDENTS MESSAGE\n\nDear OPCC members ,\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMy last five years as a member of OPCC have been very enjoyable and rewarding:\n\nIhave met many talented people and have made many friends; and have learned more about photography than I had hoped for.\n\n## SENSOR DUSI\n\nBob Huelsdonk\n\nLast January; submitted a digital projected competition print from my digital Canon D60 SLR which showed some wind generators against a plain blue sky. Two of our discerning members, Jean Timmermeister and Valerie Henschel commented that the sky had a dim but noticeable dust spot on it. had not noticed it There have been a lot of changes in my life in the last two years, and I have decided to move from western Washington where I have lived all my life to Carlsbad, California. Ihave some family in the area and had met a friend there last year. She is a world traveler and an avid photographer. But the Northwest will always be my \"home\"\n\nThe travel is still with me having traveled to Europe, Africa; South America and Antarctica since we last met and with a few weeks in Southeast Asia scheduled for February. bug\n\nIwill send Jim my email address once I settled so we can keep in contact. Thanks for the friendships and I wish all of you a Great Christmas and all the best in the New Year . get again\n\nBob Mandich\n\non my computer screen or even on the projected image until it was pointed out.\n\nReturning home; put the print on my computer screen. Indeed it showed as about a 1/2 inch, slightly darker blob (on an 8x10 image) then increased the contrast greatly; and lo and",
